# Rank 1746 / CVE-2024-36042 (CWE-287): Silverpeas's authentication service
# selected its passwordless login path by asking whether the credential
# carried a password at all. AuthenticationCredential.isPasswordSet() is the
# null-check on the password field, documented in the vulnerable revision as
# "the password isn't required to participate in an authentication; for
# example in an NTLM negotiation" -- absence of the secret is the designed
# signal for "authenticated by an external mechanism". But the
# servlet fills that same field from request.getParameter("Password")
# (AuthenticationParameters, plain-login mode), so a login request that
# simply omits the Password parameter built a passwordless credential, and
# checkAuthentication routed it to authenticateByLoginAndDomain, whose whole
# contract is "authenticates the user only by its login and the domain" -- a
# user-table equality lookup followed by a session key. The password
# verification branch had always thrown on a null password; the dispatch just
# never sent a null password there. The fixed revision (11fb5e21) gives the credential
# an explicit `authenticated` boolean set only by setRemotelyAuthenticated()
# -- called solely in the SSO/CAS/internal-authtoken/social branches, where
# the server, not the request, established the identity -- flips
# checkAuthentication to dispatch on hasBeenRemotelyAuthenticated(), and
# renames the missing-password throw to AuthenticationPwdNotAvailException.
# Remediation confirmed present at 11fb5e21; the CredentialsServlet hunk is
# reformatting only.
#
# ATTENTION, both halves of any discrimination are names the incident
# picked. The wiring-not-dataflow family of ranks 1514/1535/1540/1556/1557/
# 1593, java siblings 1733/1624/1621, with the 1380 counterweight failing:
# the remediation's only trace inside the guarded method is the call to
# setRemotelyAuthenticated/hasBeenRemotelyAuthenticated, both introduced by
# the fixing commit itself, so a negation keyed on either is the fixing
# commit's own layout (1364/1372). The mirror key -- the pre-fix predicate
# name -- is measured: a throwaway function-scope presence binding
# requiring the two authenticator spellings plus isPasswordSet (exact
# `call in [...]`, emitting code.EmptyVerifierAcceptance) reports one
# VYQL-AUTH-006 row on the core-library authentication subtree at 11fb5e21^
# (23 findings) and none at the fixed revision (22), a clean 1->0 -- and dies when
# isPasswordSet is renamed to hasPasswordGuard in the vulnerable file (0
# AUTH-006 rows), so it detects this application's spelling of the flaw,
# not the weakness. Without the guard name the same binding fires at BOTH
# revisions with the same fingerprint (c692183101a52f96): the passwordless
# lookup is legitimately reachable at both, so library vocabulary alone
# cannot discriminate. Nothing structural differs either: the two
# authenticators, the null-password throw and the request-parameter flow
# are byte-identical across the fixed revision (core-library subtree findings
# identical; core-web subtree identical except one VYQL-RF-002 fingerprint
# shifted by the reformatting), and the Java function-context tokens of
# checkAuthentication differ only in the predicate's name and the order of
# the two branches -- keying on branch order encodes the fixed revision's layout too.
# No taint path is interrupted and no construct is mishandled: vyql match
# labels the servlet's request reads (code.HttpInput) and nothing in
# AuthenticationService, and what does not exist is vocabulary for "this
# boolean predicate asserts field presence rather than an external
# authentication" -- a fact about meaning, not about a language construct,
# so there is no ENGINE-GAPS.md entry. No definition change shipped. Spec
# cve_rank1746 records the request-driven passwordless dispatch and the
# flagged form, both asserting reject VYQL-AUTH-001, VYQL-AUTH-006 and
# VYQL-AUTH-149: when passwordless-path-selection vocabulary lands, the
# first test's dispatch must flip to expect while the flagged dispatch and
# the remote-authenticated login stay reject.

test "rank1746: null password from an omitted request parameter selects the passwordless login path"
  lang java
  file core-library/src/main/java/org/silverpeas/core/security/authentication/AuthenticationService.java
  reject VYQL-AUTH-001
